---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { LEGAL_UPDATED, SITE, formatDate } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of use"
  description="Plain-language terms for using Can’t Explain: what the hall is, how to reuse it, and what not to pretend it said."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", href: "/" },
    { name: "Terms", href: "/terms" },
  ]}
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Short version: read the hall, quote it with a link, do not pretend a caption is a
      court finding. If that is too much, the back button still works.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">Updated {formatDate(LEGAL_UPDATED)}.</p>

    <h2 id="acceptance">1. Using the site</h2>
    <p>
      By using {SITE.domain} you accept these terms, plus the
      <a href="/privacy">privacy</a> page and the <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a>.
      They are part of the same deal.
    </p>

    <h2 id="what">2. What this is</h2>
    <p>
      A free, independent hall of loud claims with thin evidence. Static pages. No
      promise it will be here tomorrow, only that while it is here the files are in git.
      Nobody is entitled to uptime, a sequel, or a card about their enemy.
    </p>

    <h2 id="licence">3. What you may reuse</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Code</strong> is <a href={`${SITE.repo}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT</a>. Fork
        it, fix it, argue with it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Our writing</strong> — captions, method, these terms — may be quoted with
        attribution to {SITE.domain}. That is the price.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Logos and the name</strong> are not a costume. Do not use them to imply we
        endorse you, your party, or your thread.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Other people’s words</strong> — the quotes, headlines, and pages we cite —
        remain theirs. We link. We do not relicense the Guardian.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="hall">4. How to read a card</h2>
    <p>
      A card files a <em>claim</em>, a <em>source</em>, and a <em>receipt</em>. The
      caption is observational humour, not a second accusation and not a verdict. If you
      republish a figure or a quote from here, take the source with it. Leaving the
      receipt behind is how this hall gets new members.
    </p>

    <h2 id="conduct">5. Please do not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Scrape us into a smear pack and leave our name on it as if we signed it.</li>
      <li>Hammer the site in a way that knocks it over. It is a small static box.</li>
      <li>Pass off our captions as news copy.</li>
      <li>Upload malware, because we have nowhere to put it and would rather you didn’t try.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="warranty">6. No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The site is offered as-is. We try to get the source URL and the file right. We do
      not promise completeness, legal advice, or that a politician will have a good day.
      See the <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">7. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Corrections via
      <a href={SITE.issues}>GitHub</a>. Also: <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
